-- title:
--   Ogg's unit is fixed by the Γ(q)∩Γ₀(M') level automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q\ge 5$ and $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$, and $M'\neq 0$ divisible by neither; a field $L$ of characteristic $0$ containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ for which some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$; and an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ at level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of the unit reduction $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$. One also assumes a discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $L$, Henselian with algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\xi$ in its image, and an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible over $L$; these data come from the ambient setting and do not enter the conclusion. Let $x\in K$ have Laurent series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{q\ell}$ of the coefficient image of [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries q`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127), the series $\Delta/\Delta(q\,\cdot)$ with variable replaced by its $(q\ell)$-th power. The assertion: for every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau\in\mathrm{Aut}(K/L)$ satisfying the project's predicate `IsLevelAutAt` for $\gamma^{-1}$ at modulus $q\ell$ — namely that for all weights $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\neq 0$, every $y\in K$ whose Laurent series is the quotient of those expansions, and every complex embedding sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the complex series of $\tau y$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals that of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ — fixes $x$: $\tau x=x$.
--
--   This records the classical fact, going back to Ogg, that the modular unit $\Delta(z)/\Delta(qz)$ has level $\Gamma_0(q)$, in the form needed for the Galois-theoretic description of the field $K$: the element of $K$ whose Laurent expansion is this unit in the variable $\mathfrak q^{q\ell}$ is fixed by all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$. It is used in the construction of the labelling unit on the supersingular chart of the two-chart integral model.
-- source:
